<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-RESULTS/STANDINGS OF AFRICAN WORLD CUP QUALIFIERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-RESULTS/STANDINGS OF AFRICAN WORLD CUP QUALIFIERS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of the</p>
<p>World Cup qualifiying matches played in Africa on the weekend:</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p>In Lagos:</p>
<p>Nigeria 2 Guinea 1 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Nigeria - Daniel Amokachi (65th minute, 76th)</p>
<p>Guinea - Aboubacar Titi Camara (86th)</p>
<p>In Nairobi:</p>
<p>Kenya 4 Burkina Faso 3 (halftime 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Kenya - Mike Okoth Origi (52nd, 59th, 82nd), Francis Were</p>
<p>(67th)</p>
<p>Burkina Faso - Mamadou Zongo (15th, 65th), Firmin Sanou</p>
<p>(40th pen)</p>
<p>    Standings    P  W  D  L  F  A  PTS </p>
<p>    Nigeria	3  2  1  0  5  2  7</p>
<p>    Guinea	 3  2  0  1  6  3  6</p>
<p>    Kenya	  3  1  1  1  6  7  4</p>
<p>    Burkina Faso 3  0  0  3  3  8  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Kenya v Guinea, Nairobi, April 26</p>
<p>Burkina Faso v Nigeria, Ouagadougou, April 27</p>
<p>Group Two:</p>
<p>In Accra, Ghana:</p>
<p>Liberia 1 Egypt 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer:</p>
<p>George Weah (29th)</p>
<p>In Windhoek:</p>
<p>Namibia 1 Tunisia 2 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Namibia - Mohammed Ouseb (75th)</p>
<p>Tunisia - Taoufik Hicheri (15th), Khaled Badra (68th)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Tunisia    3  3  0  0  4  1  9</p>
<p>    Liberia    3  1  1  1  1  1  4</p>
<p>    Egypt	3  1  0  2  7  3  3</p>
<p>    Namibia    3  0  1  2  2  9  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Namibia v Egypt, Windhoek, April 26</p>
<p>Tunisia v Liberia, Tunis, April 27</p>
<p>Group Three:</p>
<p>In Pointe-Noire:</p>
<p>Congo 2 South Africa 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer:</p>
<p>Macchembe Younga (59th, 65th)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Congo	   3  2  1  0  4  1  7</p>
<p>    South Africa  3  1  1  1  1  2  4</p>
<p>    Zaire	   2  0  1  1  1  2  1</p>
<p>    Zambia	  2  0  1  1  0  1  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Zaire v Zambia, Harare, Wednesday</p>
<p>Group Four:</p>
<p>In Yaounde:</p>
<p>Cameroon 1 Zimbabwe 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Bernard Tchoutang (82nd)</p>
<p>In Luanda:</p>
<p>Angola 3 Togo 1 (halftime 2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Angola - Paulao (30th), Akwa (44th), Sousa (55th)</p>
<p>Togo - Djima Owayole (21nd)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Cameroon    3  2  1  0  5  2  7</p>
<p>    Angola	3  2  1  0  5  2  7</p>
<p>    Zimbabwe    3  1  0  2  4  3  3</p>
<p>    Togo	  3  0  0  3  3 10  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Cameroon v Togo, Yaounde, April 27</p>
<p>Zimbabwe v Angola, Harare, April 27</p>
<p>Group Five:</p>
<p>In Libreville:</p>
<p>Gabon 0 Morocco 4 (halftime 0-4)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ahmed Bahja (2nd, 5th), Bassir Salaheddine (38th, 42nd)</p>
<p>match abandoned after 55 minutes</p>
<p>In Freetown:</p>
<p>Sierra Leone 1 Ghana 1 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sierra Leone - Abubacar Kamara (23rd min own goal)</p>
<p>Ghana - Lamin Kamara (88th pen)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Morocco	2  1  1  0  6  2  4</p>
<p>    Sierra Leone 3  1  1  1  2  5  4</p>
<p>    Ghana	  3  0  3  0  4  4  3</p>
<p>    Gabon	  2  0  1  1  1  2  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Ghana v Gabon, Accra, April 27</p>
<p>Sierra Leone v Morocco, Freetown, April 27</p>
<p>The winners of each group qualify for the finals in France</p>
<p>next year.</p>
